ommand over the same implementation owner.\n\n## Approach\n\nDelete these aliases and their compatibility help/docs/tests, retaining only the canonical routes: `bridge status`, `bridge fsck`, `bridge check-access`, `bridge setup`, and `verify-identity`. Record the pre-1.0 break. The `reconcile` family is deliberately excluded; it has its own dependency-ordered container.\n\n## Scope\n\n- CLI registry and parser/help aliases\n- command references, examples, changelog, and CLI tests\n\n## Testing\n\nFor each old spelling, assert parser rejection; for each canonical spelling, assert it reaches the existing owner and preserves exit behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Each of the five approved simple aliases is absent from the CLI registry, help, docs, and examples.\n- [ ] The five canonical commands reach the same existing implementation owners and preserve their current outcomes.\n- [ ] Old spellings fail at parsing before command execution.\n- [ ] Changelog/release notes list each removed spelling and canonical replacement.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py","reason":"remove hidden alias registrations"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"remove alias dispatch compatibility"},{"path":"docs","reason":"remove obsolete CLI spellings from maintained references"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"record breaking CLI removals"},{"path":"tests","reason":"prove old parsing fails and canonical owners remain"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["janitor","cli","breaking-change","compatibility"],"ticket_id":"f773-ba24-78ea-4f0d","ticket_type":"story","title":"Remove approved simple CLI compatibility aliases","verify